IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cll-careshield`

-- CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019 (Singapore) -- the disability assessment: who may conduct and report on one
-- (s 2(1) "assessor", s 17(1)), when the Board or the Administrator may require one (ss 6(2), 7(5)(c), 16(3)(c), 21(2)(c)),
-- who decides the claim (s 16, Second Schedule Part 2), how an assessed person's six activities of daily living are counted
-- against the First and Fourth Schedules, the fee an assessor may charge (s 17(2) with the Disability Assessment Fees
-- Regulations 2020), a fraudulent assessment report (s 49), and the events for which a claim may be refused (s 16(4)(d) with
-- reg 26 of the CSHL Scheme Regulations 2020).
--
-- Edition: the Act as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLLTCA2019.txt (2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation,
-- version in force from 1 January 2026); the CareShield Life and Long-Term Care (Disability Assessment Fees) Regulations 2020
-- (S 69/2020, version in force from 31 January 2020) as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLLTCA2019-S69-2020.txt; and
-- the CareShield Life and Long-Term Care (CSHL Scheme) Regulations 2020 (S 849/2020, version in force from 1 January 2026) as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLLTCA2019-S849-2020.txt.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0278 (Haziq scenario, event from the Jun Hao or Simone scenarios (supplied-fact entry)):
-- after a stroke a claimant can no longer bathe or dress unaided and can transfer only sometimes; who assesses whether he is
-- unable to perform three of the six activities of daily living, and how is "sometimes" treated?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: how an assessor scores an activity -- what counts as "unable to perform", and in particular whether an activity
-- the person can do only sometimes counts as one he is unable to perform. Neither the Act nor either deposited regulation says;
-- that is left to the assessment practice (presumably MOH's assessment guidelines, not retrieved), and the encoding takes it as
-- an explicit open parameter `sometimes counts as unable`. Also not encoded: the qualifications and conditions of approval of
-- assessors (s 17(1) leaves both to the Minister; none retrieved); reimbursement of assessors' fees from the Fund (s 36(1), "as
-- determined by the Board"); the insured sum table (reg 25 and the Second Schedule of S 849/2020); the relevant date for a
-- s 6(1)(d) applicant (reg 2A(2)); ElderShield claims (the same Schedules apply, but this module follows CSHL claims).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example naive rows (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019 -- disability assessment`

§§ `2(1), 16, 17(1) -- who assesses and who decides`

-- s 2(1): "'assessor' means an assessor approved by the Minister under section 17(1) to conduct, and report on, disability
-- assessments".
-- s 17(1): "The Minister may, subject to such conditions as the Minister may impose, approve one or more individuals having the
-- necessary qualifications to be assessors to conduct, and report on, disability assessments under this Act." The Act does not
-- say what the qualifications are, and does not require an assessor to be a doctor; a registered medical practitioner who is not
-- approved is not an assessor.
-- s 16(1): the insured person may receive benefits if a claim is made "and the Administrator accepts the claim"; s 16(4): "The
-- Administrator may refuse a claim -- (a) if the insured person is not severely disabled". Second Schedule Part 2 puts s 16 with
-- the Administrator. So the assessor conducts and reports; the Administrator decides; the Board pays (s 18(1), Second Schedule
-- Part 1).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an assessor approved by the Minister under section 17(1)`
    `a doctor not approved as an assessor`
    `the Administrator`
    `the Board`
    `a family member`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may conduct and report on a disability assessment` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `an assessor approved by the Minister under section 17(1)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `decides whether to accept the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the Administrator` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `pays the insured sum` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `the Board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6(2), 7(5)(c), 16(3)(c), 21(2)(c) -- when an assessment may be required`

-- s 6(2): "To ascertain the disability condition of an individual for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) and (c), the Board may
-- require the individual to make a health declaration or attend a disability assessment by an assessor."
-- s 7(5)(c): on an application for cover, the Board may "require that the individual to be insured attend a disability assessment
-- by an assessor".
-- s 16(3)(c): on a claim, the Administrator may "require that the insured person attend a disability assessment by an assessor";
-- s 16(4)(c): the claim may be refused if the insured person "does not comply".
-- s 21(2)(c): on a periodic disability review, the Administrator may require the same; s 21(3): the Board may stop payment if the
-- insured person fails to comply.
-- Each is "may": the Act does not make an assessment compulsory for every claim.
DECLARE Occasion IS ONE OF
    `ascertaining disability for automatic cover under s 6(1)(b) or (c)`
    `an application for cover under s 7`
    `a claim under s 16`
    `a periodic disability review under s 21`
    `a premium deduction from MediSave`

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A Occasion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an assessment may be required` IF
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `a premium deduction from MediSave` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A Occasion
GIVETH A Person
`who may require the assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `ascertaining disability for automatic cover under s 6(1)(b) or (c)` THEN `the Board`
    WHEN `an application for cover under s 7` THEN `the Board`
    OTHERWISE `the Administrator`

§§ `First and Fourth Schedules -- scoring the six activities`

-- First Schedule: "a person is severely disabled when he or she is unable to perform 3 or more of the following activities of daily
-- living": (a) "washing himself or herself in the bath or shower (including getting into or out of the bath or shower), or washing
-- himself or herself by other means"; (b) "dressing and undressing"; (c) "feeding"; (d) "toileting"; (e) "walking, or moving, from
-- one room to another or on a level surface"; (f) "transferring himself or herself, or moving, from a bed to an upright chair or a
-- wheelchair, and vice versa".
-- Fourth Schedule: "a person is not disabled only if he or she can perform all of the following activities of daily living without
-- assistance all the time".
-- The words "all the time" appear only in the Fourth Schedule. The First Schedule says "unable to perform" and does not say whether
-- an activity the person can do sometimes is one he is "unable to perform". That is the open parameter here: with it FALSE an
-- activity done sometimes is not counted towards the three; with it TRUE it is. Under the Fourth Schedule the answer is plain:
-- an activity done only sometimes without assistance is not done "without assistance all the time", so the person is not "not
-- disabled".
DECLARE Ability IS ONE OF
    `performs it without assistance all the time`
    `performs it without assistance only sometimes`
    `cannot perform it without assistance`

DECLARE ADLs HAS
    washing IS AN Ability
    dressing IS AN Ability
    feeding IS AN Ability
    toileting IS AN Ability
    walking IS AN Ability
    transferring IS AN Ability

GIVEN `the ability` IS AN Ability, `sometimes counts as unable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`counts towards unable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ability`
    WHEN `cannot perform it without assistance` THEN 1
    WHEN `performs it without assistance only sometimes` THEN IF `sometimes counts as unable` THEN 1 ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the ability` IS AN Ability
GIVETH A NUMBER
`counts towards needing assistance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ability`
    WHEN `performs it without assistance all the time` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 1

GIVEN `the activities` IS AN ADLs, `sometimes counts as unable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of activities the person is unable to perform` MEANS
        `counts towards unable` (`the activities`'s washing) `sometimes counts as unable`
    PLUS `counts towards unable` (`the activities`'s dressing) `sometimes counts as unable`
    PLUS `counts towards unable` (`the activities`'s feeding) `sometimes counts as unable`
    PLUS `counts towards unable` (`the activities`'s toileting) `sometimes counts as unable`
    PLUS `counts towards unable` (`the activities`'s walking) `sometimes counts as unable`
    PLUS `counts towards unable` (`the activities`'s transferring) `sometimes counts as unable`

GIVEN `the activities` IS AN ADLs
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of activities needing assistance at some time` MEANS
        `counts towards needing assistance` (`the activities`'s washing)
    PLUS `counts towards needing assistance` (`the activities`'s dressing)
    PLUS `counts towards needing assistance` (`the activities`'s feeding)
    PLUS `counts towards needing assistance` (`the activities`'s toileting)
    PLUS `counts towards needing assistance` (`the activities`'s walking)
    PLUS `counts towards needing assistance` (`the activities`'s transferring)

GIVEN `the activities` IS AN ADLs, `sometimes counts as unable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` IF
    `the person is severely disabled` (`the number of activities the person is unable to perform` `the activities` `sometimes counts as unable`)

GIVEN `the activities` IS AN ADLs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is not disabled on the assessed activities` IF
    `the person is not disabled` (`the number of activities needing assistance at some time` `the activities`)

-- The question the Act leaves open bites only where the reading changes the result.
GIVEN `the activities` IS AN ADLs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the result turns on how sometimes is read` IF
        `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `the activities` TRUE
    AND (NOT `is severely disabled on the assessed activities` `the activities` FALSE)

§§ `17(2) and the Disability Assessment Fees Regulations 2020 -- the assessor's fee`

-- s 17(2): "An assessor may charge a fee, not exceeding such amount as may be prescribed, for every disability assessment that the
-- assessor conducts in respect of a person."
-- S 69/2020 reg 2: "the fees specified in the second column of the Schedule are the maximum amount that an assessor may charge for a
-- disability assessment conducted in the premises that are specified opposite in the first column". Schedule ("inclusive of GST,
-- if applicable"): "1. Assessor's place of practice $100"; "2. Any premises other than the assessor's place of practice $250".
DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `the assessor's place of practice`
    `any other premises`

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum assessment fee including GST` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the premises`
    WHEN `the assessor's place of practice` THEN 100
    OTHERWISE 250

GIVEN `the fee charged including GST` IS A NUMBER, `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assessment fee is within the cap` IF
    `the fee charged including GST` AT MOST `the maximum assessment fee including GST` `the premises`

§§ `49 -- fraudulent disability assessment`

-- s 49(1): "An assessor in making a report of a disability assessment ... must not give any information which is false, or conceal
-- any information, with the intent of causing -- (a) the individual to be given or not to be given insurance cover ...; or (b) a
-- claim made by or on behalf of the individual to be accepted or rejected".
-- (2): on conviction, "(a) to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both; and
-- (b) in addition, to a penalty equal to 4 times the relevant amount (if applicable)".
-- (3): "'relevant amount' means the amount of overpayment and the amount of assessment fee charged for the assessment" -- read here
-- as the two added together (an inference from "and").
GIVEN `false information given or information concealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `intent to affect cover or a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assessor commits an offence under section 49` IF
    `false information given or information concealed` AND `intent to affect cover or a claim`

GIVEN `the overpayment` IS A NUMBER, `the assessment fee charged` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 49 penalty` MEANS
    4 TIMES (`the overpayment` PLUS `the assessment fee charged`)

`the section 49 maximum fine` MEANS 10000

`the section 49 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS 24

§§ `16(4)(d) and CSHL Scheme Regulations 2020 reg 26 -- excluded causes`

-- s 16(4)(d): the Administrator may refuse a claim "if the insured person's severe disability arises from one or more such events or
-- occurrences as may be prescribed".
-- S 849/2020 reg 26: "the Administrator may refuse a claim if the insured person's severe disability arises from any war, invasion,
-- act of foreign enemies, hostility (whether war is declared or not), terrorist act, insurrection or military or usurped power."
-- Illness (a stroke) and an ordinary accident are not among them.
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `a stroke or other illness`
    `an accident`
    `war`
    `invasion`
    `an act of foreign enemies`
    `hostility, whether war is declared or not`
    `a terrorist act`
    `insurrection`
    `military or usurped power`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cause is a prescribed excluded event` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `a stroke or other illness` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an accident` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
